From 06e027a730ed855e256802f0f22ba7331918a803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:23:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] drm/asahi: t6050: Run the M5 Pro on bare metal with the
 J716s tables

Probe refuses the M5 Pro as having no bare-metal GPU tables: its
configuration still carries the profile, crash buffers and UAT policy of
a board that was never booted that way.

Add the 16-inch M5 Pro's (J716s) board table from its ADT:

- sgx perf-states/perf-states1 and perf-states-sram/-sram1: two
  voltage tables (perf-state-table-count 2), 14 states from 0 to
  1620 MHz. The voltages are this part's bins and differ from J714's in
  every active state (1278 MHz: 865/850 mV against 840/840).
- afr-perf-states, identical to cs-perf-states: one lane, 24 to
  1620 MHz, with SRAM at max(775 mV, core) as on J714 and J716c.
- the relative-frequency curve from gpu-perf-base-pstate 1.
- aon-ptd ptd_data_table rows RT0g/RT1g/RT0r (0x79, 0xbc, 0xce):
  J714's.
- register windows: J714's. The ADT places sgx, the four enabled AMCCs
  (amcc-enable-mask 0xf, mcc reg[14..17] + 0x104000), pmp0 reg[3], mcc
  reg[2], aon-ptd reg[0] and ane0 reg[0] where J714's slots expect them.
- active-mcc-bit-vector 0xf: the inherited MCC mask.

The rest follows the two-cluster M5 Pro (J714): core type 0x18 with
revision 4, the 2 MiB minimum parameter buffer, 4 MiB render blocks in a
4 GiB inventory, no topology words, the image's idle standby. No
controller configuration has been measured on a J716s part, so it has
none and the firmware keeps its own power budget, as J714 does on a part
whose calibration words differ. The fan curve start is J714's; the
governor is off by default.

Give the M5 Pro the M5 Max's and M5 Ultra's bare-metal profile: both
roles publish their kernel roots, the secondary's 0x40000 into
`pagetables` (as on every two-role G17, A18 Pro included; the ADT
gfx-shared-region is 0x80000), each asks for its crash log inside
`fw-data`, and the UAT policy is the Ultra's. In the 27.0, 27.2 and 27.3
G17S images, the privileged (GXF) code that builds and publishes those
roots is the G17C image's byte for byte except one call's displacement,
and in the J716s ADT each role's DATA_SHARED_RO follows its DATA, so the
fw-data span is contiguous (0x184000 bytes).

Both M5 Pro boards report ID variant 3, so the 14-inch one takes the
16-inch tables, as the 14-inch M5 Max takes J716c's. No board refuses
at probe for want of tables now, so the M5NoBareMetalTables profile
goes.

Not tested on hardware: the 27.3 stub's firmware is identified and then
refused until the M5 graph builds the 26B123 layouts.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
